{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210691,"nonce":"vb8j1zQBHFPdE0ikHyJms5pVcz8=","title":"Method-OSR intermittent null read from a list element deep in recursion","message":"GltfScene.spawnNode_ reads null from `_nodes[idx]` deep in its recursion in roughly 40% of runs (10-run sample, 2026-06-03) under default tiered mode. WLIFT_DISABLE_METHOD_OSR=1 makes it go away, which separates it from the stack-map bug where that switch has no effect.\n\nReproduces regardless of the number-parse path in @hatch:json, so switching Parser_.parseNumber_ to ByteArray.parseF64 does not introduce it, it only changes the hotness profile that exposes it. That wiring is held back until this is fixed (see the commit message of 5686f9b).\n\nSuspected family: for-in plus outer-scope local mutation under method OSR. Where to look: the method-OSR entry path in src/codegen/cranelift_backend.rs (compile_osr_entries) and how live locals are handed into the OSR entry block.","files":null}]}